<title>USA: Ascend turns software co into subsidiary.</title>
<headline>Ascend turns software co into subsidiary.</headline>
<dateline>ALAMEDA, Calif 1996-09-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ascend Communications Inc said it had merged with Subspace Communications Inc, turning it into a wholly-owned subsidiary.</p>
<p>Ascend said Subspace shareholders would receive about 90,000 of its common shares as part of the merger, which it called a &quot;pooling of interests&quot;.</p>
<p>It did not give any more details of the merger.</p>
<p>Based in Fremont, California, Subspace makes software for personal computers to get on the Internet, among other applications in telecommunications.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
